			"notes": "Gorilla Tag-style VR hand-grab locomotion for **Minecraft 26.2**. Grab surfaces with your hands and swing through the world.\n\nRequires Fabric + Vivecraft 1.3.x (PCVR).\n\n## What's new in 1.0.0.2-26.2-Release\n- **Ladders & vines** are now pass-through for your hands, so climbing no longer fights the grab physics (Vivecraft's own ladder climbing still works).\n- **Punch-mining is disabled in Creative** so blocks no longer break under your hands while you move.\n- **Mod Menu reset buttons follow the active preset**, with an `Active preset` indicator so it's clear what `reset` does.\n- **Step assist on by default.**\n- **Leaf litter** is pass-through for the hands (no more snagging on floor decoration).\n- **Hand clamp fixed** for Vivecraft 1.3.x (final-field reflection fix).\n- **Fixed the black main menu** that appeared on 1.21.9+.\n- **Fixed Real Monke** (0.5-tall hitbox) which had silently broken on 1.21.9+.\n- **Hand markers rebuilt as particles** (Mojang removed the old world-render hook in 1.21.9).\n\n## Install\nPlace the `.jar` in your `mods` folder alongside Fabric API and Vivecraft."
